From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the screens come back when the console does

`Ctrl+Alt+F2` and back locked the desktop up. The take on the way back put
DRM master back in this process and stopped there, and master is a statement
about who may program the card rather than about what the card is programmed
to.

WHAT PROGRAMMED IT IS WHOEVER HAD THE PANEL. The kernel restores its own
framebuffer the moment the last master goes -- which is the same sentence
`drm_vt_switcher.h` already used to argue that a late drop leaves a stale
console rather than a black one -- so a VT round trip ends with the CRTCs in
somebody else's mode and this process holding controller state that describes
hardware from before the switch. Every page flip into it is refused, the
atomic plane manager has no exemption for that, and `PageFlipWatchdog` answers
a refused commit with a fifteen-second timer ending in `LOG(FATAL) << "Failed
to modeset ... Crashing GPU process."` The desktop freezes and then dies, and
`0019`'s note that "nothing modesets on the way back" was the description of
this bug before it was reported.

NOTHING ELSE WAS GOING TO SEND THAT MODESET. The connectors report exactly
what they reported on the way out, so `ModesetWouldChangeAnything` -- which is
right about every hotplug, and the reason this driver no longer modesets in a
loop -- reads the next reading as "asking again cannot help". That is the same
wall a wake from suspend hits, and `DrmModeset::Relight` is already the way
past it: `0033` built it for `DrmSleep`, and a console switch back is the
second caller it always needed.

So `StepVtSwitch` grows one action and one cell: a take that succeeded from
`kTaking` now answers `kRelightDisplay` instead of `kNothing`, and `Perform`
runs `DrmModeset::Relight`. AFTER the take has answered and not before it,
because `TakeDisplayControl` is what puts master back in this process and
`has_master()` back in the GPU's -- a modeset ahead of either is the `EACCES`
the rest of this path exists to stop committing.

EXACTLY ONE CELL, AND THE TEST SAYS SO. A modeset is a commit on the card, so
a relight asked for from any state that does not hold the console is a commit
over somebody else's frame, and one asked for on an edge that repeats is the
modeset loop again. `DrmVtSwitcherTest` walks the whole table and asserts no
other cell lights anything.

The wiring is this patch's whole edit to a file Chromium owns: `modeset_` is
built ahead of `vt_switcher_` in `InitScreen` and declared ahead of it, so the
pointer is live for the switcher's life and the switcher is destroyed first --
the same seam `sleep_` already takes.

Guidelines audited: docs/guidelines/TESTING.md, docs/guidelines/ERRORS.md,
docs/guidelines/CONTROL_FLOW.md, docs/guidelines/FUNCTIONS.md,
docs/guidelines/FILES.md. Change complies.

Co-Authored-By: Connor Prussin <connor@prussin.net>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FHahS8JpYFNtfjYsdorEfp
---
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc
index 6a0765726091..3469dd6f6e39 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/ozone_platform_drm.cc
@@ -127,8 +127,16 @@ class OzonePlatformDrm : public OzonePlatform {
     // key in the desktop is dispatched through, and it exists by now:
     // `InitializeUI` builds it and a screen is not initialized before a
     // platform is.
+    //
+    // AND `modeset_`, because the console this session comes back to is not
+    // the one it left: whoever had the panel in between programmed the card,
+    // and master says nothing about what it is programmed to. The take is
+    // answered and then the screens are lit again, which is the difference
+    // between a desktop that survives `Ctrl+Alt+F<n>` and one that locks up
+    // on the way back. See `domicile/drm_vt_switcher.h`.
     vt_switcher_ = std::make_unique<DrmVtSwitcher>(
-        CreateNativeDisplayDelegate(), event_factory_ozone_.get());
+        CreateNativeDisplayDelegate(), event_factory_ozone_.get(),
+        modeset_.get());
 
     // And the machine this console is on, which can go to sleep under it. A
     // suspend takes nothing away from this session -- logind pauses no device
@@ -476,7 +484,8 @@ class OzonePlatformDrm : public OzonePlatform {
   // delegate it holds.
   std::unique_ptr<DrmModeset> modeset_;
   // And after event_factory_ozone_ for the same kind of reason: it observes
-  // that event source for as long as it lives.
+  // that event source for as long as it lives. And after modeset_, which it
+  // asks to light the screens again when the console comes back.
   std::unique_ptr<DrmVtSwitcher> vt_switcher_;
   // And after modeset_, which it holds and asks to light the screens again
   // when the machine wakes up.
